On Thu, 10 May 2007, Moonsilence wrote:

> The item spoilers tell me the buying price of items, but if I own and
> unidentified item (for example a scroll) and bring it to a shop, I will
> only know the selling price (when i drop the scroll in the shop, the
> shopkeep offers me X zorkmids).

In general, the selling price is half of the base price. Randomly (per
interaction, not per item), the shopkeeper might offer one fourth less.

All about price-identifying is explained in the spoiler at
<www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~damerell/games/nhid.html>.

